he menu is visually visible.","repair_strategy":"Update the syncState method to conditionally apply aria-hidden only when the menu button is visible (mobile viewport) and the menu is not open; otherwise ensure the menu is exposed (aria-hidden=false).","edits":[{"path":"src/govuk/components/header/header.js","sha256":"33e331b7a1f44087522e90d1e295dbc0f915c8b8a82e8afd57a794d21fff4424","before":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', !isVisible)\n}","after":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  // Determine if menu should be hidden from assistive tech\n  var hidden = !isVisible;\n  // If menu button is not displayed (desktop), menu should be visible\n  if (this.$menuButton && window.getComputedStyle(this.$menuButton).display === 'none') {\n    hidden = false;\n  }\n  this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', hidden);\n}"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Navigation links will be exposed in the accessibility tree as links with correct accessible names, enabling screen reader and keyboard users to reach them.","functional_risks":["Reliance on computed style may fail if the menu button's display property is changed dynamically in an unexpected way.","If the CSS for the header changes, the condition may need adjustment."],"verification_requirements":["Verify that at desktop width the navigation links have role link and names 'Apply', 'Renew a licence', 'Fishing rules'.","Verify that at mobile width the menu button toggles the navigation visibility and correctly sets aria-hidden and aria-expanded.","Ensure that opening and closing the menu via the button still works as expected.","Confirm no regression in the header's visu